cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Grey-Box Digital Twin for Risk Monitoring and Predictive Control
  of a Small Modular Dual Fluid Reactor
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from
  this file, together with the thesis it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Leonardo Andrés
    family-names: Miqueles Leiva
    affiliation: Politecnico di Milano
    email: leonardoandres.miqueles@polimi.it
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/leomiq/dt_riskcontrol_smdfr'
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a grey-box digital twin for an SMDFR:
  a reduced-order plant model, a grey-box virtual sensor for the peak
  cladding temperature, an Importance-Sampling Monte Carlo Dynamic
  Event Tree for dynamic risk assessment, and a model predictive
  controller whose objective carries a deterministic-safety-margin
  soft constraint.
keywords:
  - digital twin
  - grey-box modelling
  - risk monitoring
  - dynamic event tree
  - importance sampling
  - model predictive control
  - safety margin
  - small modular reactor
